This is my first ascension in the 2005 Tournament - not the last, I hope.
This Samurai didn't have much trouble until the point where, worrying
about the Quest, he found the bones of a Valkyrie with SDSM and a spare
magic lamp for CoMR. I couldn't pick up the Orb of Weight but even that at
that point I pretty well had it made; I WoDeathed the Nemesis, burned the
Castle wand (0:1) and another magic lamp (and I had a 4th spare at the
end) on some slightly unusual gear, since I already had the vital stuff.

I levteled down to the bottom with Asmodeus, but accidentally killed him a
few levels up, so I did have to explore most of Gehennom. However, I found
Vlad's stairs randomly, so didn't have to make an exhaustive search of the
levels in range. I felt I had all the stuff I needed so didn't even
bother, say, clearing out Orcus. The mysterious force was a bit of a pain
but Gehennom was quite short, so even in spite of difficulty hitting
Rodney I didn't run out of WoDeath zaps. Eventually I made it out - not
without a nervous moment seeing a green slime on Jubilex and realising I'd
forgotten to bring a wand of fire, but I just evaded contact (and could
always have levelported to Vlad's and prayed).

None of the planes presented a serious problem, although I had tediously
long walks on Earth and Fire; Air never got me down to less than half HP
thanks to resting up in vortices, and since I had AoMB and an oilskin sack
I could levitate across Water without worrying about evasion. I did Famine
first - very quickly with the Plane not too full - but that was no good; I
got into Death quickly, but decided it would be a shame not to bring the
guardian angel (I wasn't under any threat) so went back for it.

